        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add accessTier to CLI MESSAGESENT analytics",
        "summary": "Added `accessTier` property to `MESSAGE_SENT` event tracking in `cli/src/commands/router.ts`. Retrieves tier from `useFreebuffSessionStore` state, defaulting to 'unknown' if session or tier is missing. Applies only to Freebuff CLI surface. No action required.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:06:50.150Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the Freebuff command-line tool to chat with an AI, the assistant now quietly records which subscription level you have when you send a message. Your account's access tier is sent along with your message data; if the system can't find your session or tier for any reason, it just logs 'unknown'. You won't see anything new on screen, but the people who build and improve Freebuff can now use your tier information to understand how different subscriber levels use the tool.",
